  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a consistent relationship between Glycine and Glyatl2, mediated through Glyatl1. Glycine binds to Glyatl1, which then participates in multiple enzymatic activities, including N-acyltransferase activity, amino acid conjugation of benzoic acid, and conjugation of benzoate with glycine. These activities are all part of a broader metabolic pathway that ultimately leads to Glyatl2 being a participant in these processes. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, reliable connection, with Glyatl1 acting as a central hub in the interaction network. The shared involvement of Glyatl1 in different enzymatic functions suggests that it may be a key player in the metabolic transformation of glycine, potentially influencing Glyatl2 through these pathways. The integration of these evidence points to Glycine as a substrate that indirectly affects Glyatl2 via Glyatl1, highlighting a complex but well-defined interaction.",
